   "say": "As a kid, Adolf wasn't very social. He found it hard to connect.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "say": "When he went to a summer camp...",
   "gap": 0.35
  },
  {
   "say": "Danny said: \"Welcome to my camp!\"",
   "gap": 0.3
  },
  {
   "say": "Hitler answered: \"It is mine.\"",
   "gap": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Danny said: \"OK, you can join. You just have to share.\"",
   "gap": 0.3
  },
  {
   "say": "Hitler answered: \"This camp is mine.\"",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "say": "And then he said: \"My camp, mine <<ˈ|k|ɑː|m|p|f>>. Potato, <<p|ə|ˈ|t|ɑː|t|oʊ>>, right?\"",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "say": "He never got it. He had issues with possessives.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "say": "Also with possessions.",
   "gap": 0.45
  },
  {
   "say": "Honestly, he was a bit possessive.",
   "gap": 0.35
  },
  {
   "say": "He was a bit possessed.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "say": "Later we realised it wasn't only his English. He was really struggling.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "say": "Which is why he called his book... Mein <<ˈ|k|ɑː|m|p|f>>.",
   "gap": 0.75
  },
  {
   "say": "My Struggle.",
   "gap": 0.6
  },
  {
   "say": "The struggle was real... maybe because",
   "gap": 0.0
  }
